{"name":"Darkest Dungeon","hex":"#660011","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"darkest","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["superlative form of dark: most dark"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/darkest"},{"term":"dungeon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An underground prison or vault, typically built underneath a castle.","The low area between two drumlins."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To imprison in a dungeon."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dungeon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Darkest Dungeon","blocks":[{"text":"Darkest Dungeon is a roguelike role-playing video game developed and published by Red Hook Studios. The game was first released for Microsoft Windows and OS X in January 2016, which followed a year-long early access development period. Later that year, it was released for PlayStation 4, PlayStation Vita, and Linux, with a port for iOS being released in 2017, and ports for Nintendo Switch and Xbox One being released by 2018."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8d/Darkest_Dungeon_Logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkest_Dungeon","wikidata":"Q16259390"},{"title":"Dungeon","blocks":[{"text":"A dungeon is a type of prison, usually an underground room or cell, in which prisoners are held. Dungeons are generally associated with medieval castles. They are closely connected in concept both to the prison and the oubliette, and the words are sometimes used interchangeably. In the popular imagination, a dungeon is claustrophobic, strong, damp, and located in a castle under the direct control of a medieval lord. This intentional unpleasantness and personal control over a dungeon contrasts to the modern prison, which provides a civil function."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/BlarneyCastle5.jpg/330px-BlarneyCastle5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dungeon","wikidata":"Q89753"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/04/Darkest-dungeon-03.jpg/330px-Darkest-dungeon-03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/04/Darkest-dungeon-03.jpg/330px-Darkest-dungeon-03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In-game screenshot of a typical battle scene. The character in the foreground is performing her combat animation against the enemy party on the right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADarkest-dungeon-03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/dc/CrimsonCourtBattle.jpg/330px-CrimsonCourtBattle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/dc/CrimsonCourtBattle.jpg/330px-CrimsonCourtBattle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In-game screenshot of a battle scene with the new DLC encounter boss The Fanatic  ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACrimsonCourtBattle.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg/500px-Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg/1280px-Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg/500px-Muzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A dungeon door in the Zrinski Castle in Čakovec, Croatia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuzej_Me%C4%91imurja%2C_%C4%8Cakovec_-_vrata_tamnice_u_Starom_gradu_Zrinskih.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Oubliettes.Bastille.png/330px-Oubliettes.Bastille.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Oubliettes.Bastille.png/330px-Oubliettes.Bastille.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diagram of an alleged oubliette found in the Bastille prison in Paris, from Viollet-le-Duc (1854–1868).[9][10][11] the commentary [by le Duc?] speculates that the structure depicted, may actually have been an ice well built to keep ice.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOubliettes.Bastille.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Warrek%E2%80%99s_Nest.jpg/500px-Warrek%E2%80%99s_Nest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Warrek%E2%80%99s_Nest.jpg/1280px-Warrek%E2%80%99s_Nest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Warrek%E2%80%99s_Nest.jpg/500px-Warrek%E2%80%99s_Nest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A \"dungeon\" map created for a tabletop roleplaying game","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWarrek%E2%80%99s_Nest.jpg"}],"sounds":{"dungeon":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/66/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-dungeon.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"ty